 "description": "BIGVILLE R16 (block 264000) -- EVICTION IS ENFORCEMENT WITH A DOER WHO FEELS IT (de-magicalizes R7's auto-seizure). bc_evict is the ACT: a doer -enforces_for-> rental must REACH the home (house -at_home_cell-> cell, R1) with arrears past term -> r16_evicted=1, tenant.homeless=1 (reusing R7 bf_homeless_affect for the family's distress), did_evict++. No doer / no reach -> the eviction does NOT happen at the same arrears. bc_moral_injury (HEADLINE) is the perpetrator-side MIRROR: a doer with empathy (w_supergraph>0) takes an affective HIT (arousal up/valence down = guilt) performing it; bc_no_injury is the psychopath path (w=0, John) closing the books with ZERO injury -- ablate empathy and the injury vanishes. bc_pick_cheapest_hands is the emergent offload read-off: the graph's Argmax over candidate doers by -(ask_wage + w_supergraph*injury_mag) writes the cost-minimizing doer's empathy to picked_w (the gb_choose_give scalar pattern -- no computed-node edge) so the banality of eviction can be MEASURED, not scripted. Every decision a RULE; composes existing Terms (incl Argmax/Neighbours); zero new Rust.",
